# Issue #31 direct Coder Apply — class doctrine as role I/O contracts

Implement the current GitHub Issue #31 authority, its owner key-grammar resolution, and the converged Judge receipts. There is no Plan phase. Work test-first where Issue #31 authorizes logic tests; commit forward and submit through `ak_coder_output`.

## Behavior

### Judge contract

Add optional `classes[]` entries `{name, owner, boundary, disposition}` to Judge output. Each string is nonblank. Class `name` follows the owner-ratified shared grammar: comma-free, exact/case-sensitive/no normalization, and unique within the array. Ordering has no semantic force. `continue` requires nonempty `classes`; `converged` and `escalate` forbid it. Preserve required `fix.summary` for `continue`, existing note/decisionGate behavior, exact-object contracts, package-contract validation, audit, dist/package surfaces, and backward behavior outside the intentionally changed `continue` shape.

### Fixer contract

Add optional `classesRepaired[]` entries `{name, searchScope, exceptions:[{where, reason}]}` to Fixer completion output. Names use the same grammar and are unique; strings are nonblank; `classesRepaired` itself is nonempty when present; `exceptions` may be empty. `planned` and `refused` forbid `classesRepaired`; `completed` may carry it. Coder output remains exactly unchanged and cannot carry it. The package does not inspect opaque Markdown to decide contextual presence or cross-input equality: caller mechanically enforces presence/absence and exact order-insensitive set equality against its typed Judge receipt, as Judge recheck O1 ruled. Preserve commitSha/report/status behavior.

### Reviewer scope input

Add optional CLI `--ak-review-scope-keys <comma-separated keys>`. Absence means full review. Presence with empty input, zero parsed keys, a blank/whitespace-only token, a comma-bearing/unrepresentable token, or exact duplicate keys fails during activation before any Reviewer child starts. Preserve exact case and token bytes; do not normalize. Inject the accepted key list deterministically into the parent Reviewer system prompt and into every Standards/Spec child system prompt through the existing construction seam. Keep task opaque, capabilities/tool grants unchanged, model/provider inheritance unchanged, and one sibling-parallel batch unchanged.

### Documentation transition

Remove `docs/class-repair-playbook.md` and its single `CLAUDE.md` pointer in the same change. Add a README usage section explaining how callers compose the three typed contracts without prescribing mandatory ordering or routing. Preserve ADR 0010. ADR 0015, ADR 0016, and the CONTEXT term are already merged into this branch; retain them.

